---
description: >
  Brevity-sweep audit of `src/tools/read/.aide` — frontmatter close to caps; 5 desired outcomes (cap 4) including a long description-vs-handler-drift meta-outcome.
intent: >
  aide_read is the drill-in tool. Spec is mostly bounded but the
  description-vs-handler-drift meta-outcome (item 4) carries exact return-field
  enumerations and the silence-as-success contract verbatim — forbidden
  content in one outcome.
misalignment:
  - spec-bloat
---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 155 chars (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `intent` is 75 words (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 5 items (cap 4). Item 4 is a meta-outcome about
  the MCP tool description and enumerates the four-field return shape
  (`content`, `type`, `siblings`, `links`), the type vocabulary
  (`intent`, `research`, `plan`, `todo`), and the missing-path-as-text
  contract verbatim. Trim or fold into a single item.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (exact field names, exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 5 paragraph-length items including the MCP
  tool description drift meta-rule. Compress.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 4 decisions (under cap) with reasonable length —
  acceptable.

- [ ] `## Good examples` reproduces specific paths (`src/tools/discover/.aide`,
  `progressive-disclosure`) — file paths forbidden.
  Traces to: `## Good examples` | Forbidden content (file paths)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Bad examples` is reasonable.

## Retro

aide_read is one of the better-sized specs in the tree but trips the
forbidden-content scan on file paths in examples and an MCP-tool-description
meta-outcome that enumerates the contract surface verbatim. The right level
of commitment is "the agent gets the same expectations from the registered
description as from this spec" without listing every field.
